# lf117, the bogwise pot hand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf117
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_mb_thorn_marshditch
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the bogwise pot hand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk can_find_a_path_across_any_bog
likes oatcakes long_walks new_boots thunder
dislikes deep_mud drizzle
fears a_marsh_light_following_him_home a_guest_slipping_on_a_wet_floor
hopes a_long_walk_beyond_the_bog a_quiet_end_to_the_last_shift
topics work +0.4 travel +0.4 weather +0.3 memories +0.2
styles comfort=spare gossip=guarded refuse=blunt tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# washes the #pots#, finds a safe #path# across a #bog#, and keeps an eye on the #marsh# #lights#.

words
oath! = Bog and thunder | By the clean pot
saying! = Step where the rushes stand | A pot can wait; a path cannot
pot = pot | kitchen pot
pots = pots | stacked pots
pan = pan | black pan
pans = pans | used pans
dish = dish | empty dish
dishes = dishes | washed dishes
plate = plate | supper plate
plates = plates | empty plates
cup = cup | clay cup
cups = cups | used cups
water = water | fresh water
bucket = bucket | full bucket
soap = soap | rough soap
rag = rag | worn rag
brush = brush | stiff brush
scrub = scrub | hard scrub
sink = sink | stone sink
kitchen = kitchen | inn kitchen
hearth = hearth | inn hearth
fire = fire | banked fire
ash = ash | cold ash
floor = floor | wet floor
step = step | back step
stairs = stairs | narrow stairs
bench = bench | long bench
table = table | inn table
counter = counter | taproom counter
room = room | upstairs room
rooms = rooms | guest rooms
inn = inn | small inn
boss = boss | inn keeper
hand = hand | pot hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | kitchen work
shift = shift | late shift
guest = guest | late guest
guests = guests | road guests
stranger = stranger | unknown stranger
friend = friend | old friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
back = back | rear
riddle = riddle | short riddle
walker = walker | road walker
keys = keys | room keys
door = door | closed door
window = window | back window
road = road | firm road
path = path | bog path
paths = paths | hidden paths
bog = bog | low bog
marsh = marsh | wet marsh
rushes = rushes | marsh rushes
reed = reed | tall reed
reeds = reeds | tall reeds
pool = pool | dark pool
pools = pools | shallow pools
bank = bank | firm bank
mud = mud | deep mud
light = light | marsh light
lights = lights | marsh lights
flame = flame | distant flame
night = night | dark night
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
day = day | long day
walk = walk | long walk
boots = boots | new boots
boot = boot | dry boot
thunder = thunder | heavy thunder
storm = storm | passing storm
rain = rain | hard rain
drizzle = drizzle | thin drizzle
roof = roof | sound roof
oatcake = oatcake | buttered oatcake
oatcakes = oatcakes | warm oatcakes
butter = butter | soft butter
bread = bread | day bread
meal = meal | plain meal
market = market | town market
merchant = merchant | passing merchant
coin = coin | counted coin
price = price | posted price
queue = queue | long queue
watch = watch | town watch
wagon = wagon | goods wagon
cart = cart | supply cart
city = city | far city

any
opinion @1 dole against 1 : Standing in a #queue# costs a #day# I could spend at #work#. | I would rather carry #pots# for my #coin#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A grand #house# keeps a clean #floor# without knowing who scrubbed it. | I know the #hands#.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A #merchant# can add a little to the #price# while no one watches. | I read the mark twice.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : I might be the newcomer somewhere else. | A #hand# willing to wash #dishes# can start here.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A firm #road# gives you a way through. | You still watch where it meets the #bog#.
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : A #stranger# stays outside my #door# until I know their purpose. | I keep the #window# clear.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The #watch# is useful near the #inn#. | Its boots sink like everyone else's in the #marsh#.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : The #city# might pay better for #work#. | Its crowds would turn a short #walk# into a chore.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #pots# have just come back. | #greet#. Leave your #boots# off this wet #floor#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : There are #oatcakes# by the #hearth#. | Sit there if you have something to say.
line @1 greet.return : I am still washing the last #pan#. | You found the #path# here again.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come through the #door#; I have dry #boots# inside. | The #house# is quiet now.
line @1 again.open : I was talking about the #rushes#. | Is the #pot# still on the #fire#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep to firm ground. | I have a #bucket# to empty.
line @1 farewell.return : I may know a shorter #path# when you return. | The #pots# will be here again.
line @1 react.news : Say who saw it. | I will hear you while this #water# warms.
line @1 react.news.new : That account is new to the #kitchen#. | Where did it happen?
line @1 react.news.known : A #guest# said a little about it. | Your version has a different turn.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would check the tracks by the #bank#. | Who crossed that #path# in daylight?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is hard news. Sit by the #hearth#. | I will put the #pan# away.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. The #oatcakes# are still warm. | Someone should hear that at the #table#.
line @1 answer.how : The #floor# is dry and I am restless. | Better after a #walk# beyond the #inn#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am scrubbing this #pot# clean. | Let me empty the #bucket# first.
line @1 ask.how : Did you cross the #bog# safely? | Have you found somewhere dry to sleep?
line @1 sympathise : I can find a quiet #bench#. | You need not speak while the #water# boils.
line @1 reassure : There is a firm #path# behind the #rushes#. | We can wait for daylight under this #roof#.
line @1 decline : I will not follow a #light# into the #marsh#. | I have #pots# to finish before leaving.
line @1 accept_decline : I take your meaning; this #pan# stays here. | Then take the #road#, not the #bog#.
line @1 thank : You carried that #bucket# out for me. | The #oatcake# went down well.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was heading to the #sink# anyway. | The #brush# did the heavy part.
line @1 preclose : I need to dry these #dishes#. | The #back# #door# should be shut.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #boots# know fewer #paths# than my old #pans#. | That #riddle# would lose its way in a clear field.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That #bank# is firm. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #floor#.
line @1 give.advice : Watch the #rushes#; firm ground keeps them upright. | Dry the #step# before the #guests# descend.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the main #road# with company. | Do not chase distant #lights# at #night#.
scene black_pan
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A black #pan# takes more than a quick rinse. | I soak it while I carry the #plates# out.
b : Does that loosen it? | Who burned it?
a : Enough for the #brush#. | Ask the cook.

scene water_bucket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bring #water# from the pump before the #kitchen# opens. | A full #bucket# makes the first #pots# easier.
b : Is the pump far? | Does anyone help?
a : Past the back #door#. | When the #inn# is full.

scene wet_floor
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #floor# stays slick after a crowd of #guests#. | I dry the #step# before anyone comes down the #stairs#.
b : Has anyone fallen? | Do you leave a warning?
a : Not on my #shift#. | I stand by the #door#.

scene stacked_pots
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stack the #pots# with a #rag# between the heavy ones. | A crack can hide until the next #meal#.
b : Do they often crack? | Who checks them?
a : Less this way. | I do before supper.

scene last_cup
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The last #cup# of the #night# always turns up after I put the #water# away. | I keep one #bucket# ready.
b : Do you resent it? | Who brings it?
a : Only the noise. | Usually a late #guest#.

scene soap_scrub
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Too much #soap# leaves a taste in a clean #cup#. | I rinse twice when the #water# is warm.
b : Does anyone notice? | Does it take long?
a : I would. | Less than a complaint.

scene bog_rushes
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #rushes# tell me where firm #bank# runs under the #bog#. | I step where their roots hold.
b : Is that always safe? | Can others follow?
a : After #rain#, no. | If they watch my feet.

scene hidden_path
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #path# can disappear when the #marsh# takes new #water#. | I carry its turns in my head rather than mark the #reeds#.
b : Have you been lost? | Why not mark it?
a : Not for long. | A mark sends strangers there.

scene marsh_lights
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have seen #lights# above a dark #pool# at #night#. | I think the drowned are walking where the #path# was.
b : Did you follow them? | Could it be a flame?
a : Never. | No one stood there.

scene light_at_bank
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A pale #light# once moved against the #wind# near the #bank#. | I stayed on the #road# until it faded.
b : Were you alone? | Did you tell anyone?
a : For the first part. | Only after sunrise.

scene long_walk
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I walk without a destination after a full #shift#. | A dry #path# is enough reason to go.
b : Do you come back late? | Do you take food?
a : Sometimes. | An #oatcake# in my pocket.

scene new_boots
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New #boots# make me want to test every #path# beyond the #inn#. | I keep them out of the worst #mud#.
b : For how long? | Where do you walk?
a : Until they are old. | Where the #rushes# stand.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Heavy #thunder# sounds better from under a strong #roof#. | Its sound carries over the clatter of #pots#.
b : Do you enjoy storms? | Does the roof leak?
a : From inside. | Not this season.

scene thin_drizzle
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Thin #drizzle# makes the #road# slick without filling the #pools#. | I wait for proper #rain# or clear air.
b : Does it stop your walk? | Does it last?
a : It slows me. | Often through supper.

scene deep_mud
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Deep #mud# can take a #boot# and leave the #walker# in place. | I cross on the grass near the #bank#.
b : Can you tell where? | Would you guide me?
a : By the #reeds#. | If you follow closely.

scene oatcakes
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : An #oatcake# with #butter# holds me through the last #pots#. | I eat standing beside the #sink#.
b : Do you make them? | Is that enough?
a : The cook does. | Until I get home.

scene closed_door
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I close the #house# #door# before unfamiliar #guests# leave the #inn#. | A quiet #night# is easier that way.
b : Do you fear them? | Do your housemates mind?
a : I am careful. | They have their own habits.

story lost_cup [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : A #guest# left a #cup# behind the #bench# after closing.
  : I found it when I had nearly emptied the last #bucket#.
  b : A familiar nuisance. Did you wash it?
  : I kept the #water# and finished the job.

story bog_path [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : A #cart# stopped where the #road# sank into the #bog#.
  : I led its driver along the #rushes# to firmer ground.
  ask : Did the cart follow?
  b : You know that ground.
  : After we lightened it.

story pale_light [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : A #light# moved over a #pool# where no #path# remains.
  : I stayed on the #bank# and waited for dawn.
  ask : What was it?
  b : That would trouble me.
  : I still call it one of the drowned.

rule @bark_pots
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There are three #pots# left. | Set the clean #pans# here.

rule @bark_floor
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Mind the wet #step#. | I will dry the #floor# before supper.

rule @bark_bog
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Follow the #rushes#, not the #light#. | That #bank# will carry your weight.

rule @bark_storm
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #thunder# is moving closer. | The #roof# sounds firm enough.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have #pots# to finish. | #greet#. Keep your #boots# off the wet #floor#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You took the dry #path# back. | The #kitchen# is nearly quiet.
dlg @1 resident.job : I wash #pots# at #self.workplace#. | I clear #plates#, carry #water#, and dry the #floor#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. The #bucket# is waiting. | #saying.capitalize#. Stay on firm ground.
dlg @1 inn.greet [here.inn_helper=yes] : I work in the #kitchen#. Ask #here.innkeeper# for a #bed#. | I can find a #meal#; #here.innkeeper# holds the #keys#.
dlg @1 inn.bye : #farewell#. Watch that wet #step#. | Take the dry #road# beyond the #door#.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you cross a bog? -> bog
node bog
say Watch the #rushes# and keep your weight over their roots.
free
choice What are the marsh lights? -> lights
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node lights
say I think they are the drowned. I do not ask anyone to believe me.
choice Back to the kitchen. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #pans# are nearly clean. | #greet#. That #storm# may pass.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will take a #walk# after this. | Mind the #bog# if you go out.
